SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"UN Secretary-General's remarks to Security Council meeting on Ukraine","publisher":"United Nations in Ukraine","publication_date":"2022-09-22","url":"https://ukraine.un.org/en/200613-un-secretary-generals-remarks-security-council-meeting-ukraine","claim":"The UN Secretary-General said Russia's war in Ukraine was moving away from peace, that annexation by threat or force violates the UN Charter, and that Russian bombardment had killed and injured thousands of civilians.","locator":"speech lines 65-79, 83-84, 150-154","source_type":"IGO","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official UN speech page with direct contemporaneous remarks and quantified civilian-impact framing.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers the 2022 war through September 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Russian Federation conduct under Putin's command authority.","contrary_evidence":["Russia argued the war and referenda were defensive and lawful."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.4","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russian sham referenda in Ukraine: UK statement to the OSCE","publisher":"GOV.UK / Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","publication_date":"2022-09-29","url":"https://www.gov.uk/government/speeches/russian-sham-referenda-in-ukraine-uk-statement-to-the-osce","claim":"The UK said Russia's September 2022 referenda were a brazen attempt to justify an illegal land grab, conducted under armed coercion and followed by partial mobilization and nuclear threats.","locator":"speech lines 94-118","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official government transcript delivered at the OSCE with specific factual allegations and policy framing.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers late-September 2022 annexation and mobilization.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Putin-led Russian state actions and occupation structures.","contrary_evidence":["Russian officials claimed the referenda were legitimate and reflected self-determination."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.3","2B.6","2B.8","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Vladimir Putin's false war claims","publisher":"DW","publication_date":"2022-02-25","url":"https://amp.dw.com/en/fact-check-do-vladimir-putins-justifications-for-going-to-war-against-ukraine-add-up/a-60917168","claim":"DW concluded that Putin's claims that Russia had to defend itself, denazify Ukraine, and invoke Article 51 were false and unsupported as a justification for the invasion.","locator":"fact-check sections on 'Is Russia's attack a defense case under the UN Charter?' and 'Was there a genocide in Ukraine?'","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct fact-checking article that evaluates Putin's stated justifications against public record and international law.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly addresses the opening of the 2022 invasion.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed directly to Putin's public justification narrative.","contrary_evidence":["Russia maintained the operation was defensive and aimed at protecting Donbas."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.3","2B.6"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia invades Ukraine: What you need to know","publisher":"DW","publication_date":"2022-02-24","url":"https://www.dw.com/en/russia-invades-ukraine-what-you-need-to-know/a-60895337","claim":"DW reported that Putin announced a 'special military operation' as Russian forces launched a wide-ranging attack on Ukraine, and that diplomatic efforts were still underway when the invasion began.","locator":"section 'Putin announces special operation' and the surrounding lead paragraphs","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous war report summarizing the invasion announcement and collapse of diplomacy.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers 24 February 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed directly to Putin's invasion decision.","contrary_evidence":["Russia framed the action as a limited operation responding to Ukrainian aggression."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.2","2B.7"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Fact check: Putin's lies about Ukraine war","publisher":"DW","publication_date":"2022-07-10","url":"https://amp.dw.com/en/fact-check-putins-lies-about-the-bombing-of-ukraine/a-62419749","claim":"DW reported that Putin's claim that the Russian army did not strike civilian facilities was contradicted by documented Russian attacks on civilian targets, including Bucha and other urban sites.","locator":"sections 'Hard evidence of Russian attacks on civilian targets' and 'Kramatorsk train station air strike'","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Evidence-based fact-check using UN reporting, media documentation, and incident examples.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers 2022 civilian-harm conduct.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Russian military conduct under Putin's war decision.","contrary_evidence":["The Kremlin denied targeting civilians and described strikes as military-only."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Talk of compromise on both sides lifts hope for Russia-Ukraine breakthrough","publisher":"Euronews (Reuters)","publication_date":"2022-03-17","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/03/17/uk-ukraine-crisis","claim":"Reuters reported that Russia and Ukraine were discussing neutral-status and security-guarantee ideas, but Ukraine still sought a ceasefire and Russian troop withdrawal, showing that a negotiated path existed in March 2022.","locator":"lines 641-670","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters reporting on live negotiations and the positions of both sides.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers the March 2022 peace-process window.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Putin and Russian negotiators as part of the Russian negotiating position.","contrary_evidence":["The same report notes Russian bombardment continued while talks were occurring."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Explainer-Peace talks on Ukraine: Russia's red lines unchanged","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-03-30","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/explainerpeace-talks-on-ukraine-russias-red-lines-unchanged-2794877","claim":"Reuters reported that Russia and Ukraine were still talking about a peace deal in March 2022, but remained far apart, while Putin insisted the operation was needed because the United States was threatening Russia through Ukraine.","locator":"lines 406-415","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters explainer summarizing contemporaneous negotiations and Putin's stated rationale.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly concerns March 2022 diplomacy and justification claims.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Putin's public rationale and Russian negotiation posture.","contrary_evidence":["Ukraine said Russia was pursuing an imperial land grab and false genocide claims."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.2","2B.3","2B.6","2B.7"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia reframes war goals as Ukrainians advance near Kyiv","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-03-24","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/world-news/ukraine-urges-halt-to-russias-assault-as-biden-heads-to-poland-2791645","claim":"Reuters reported that Moscow was scaling back its ambitions after setbacks near Kyiv and shifting focus to the Donbass, indicating an escalation-to-consolidation change rather than a clear peace turn.","locator":"lines 427-429","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters reporting on a major shift in stated Russian war aims.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly reflects Russian conduct in late March 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Russian leadership and defense ministry strategy under Putin.","contrary_evidence":["Russia described the change as completing the first phase of a limited operation."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.8","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"What Does Russia’s 'Partial Mobilization' Mean?","publisher":"CSIS","publication_date":"2022-09-26","url":"https://www.csis.org/analysis/what-does-russias-partial-mobilization-mean","claim":"CSIS assessed that Putin's 21 September partial mobilization was a major escalation forced by battlefield reverses and personnel shortages, and that it was part of a strategy to outlast Ukraine and its supporters.","locator":"lines 247-260","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Expert analysis from a major policy institute, closely tied to contemporaneous facts but still interpretive.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly covers the September 2022 mobilization decision.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Putin's political and military strategy.","contrary_evidence":["The Kremlin framed mobilization as defensive and limited to reservists."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.8","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ukraine war: Putin declares partial military mobilisation to bolster Russia's troop numbers","publisher":"Euronews (AP)","publication_date":"2022-09-21","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/09/21/putin-declares-partial-military-mobilisation-to-bolster-ukraine-war-effort","claim":"Euronews reported that Putin ordered partial mobilization to support the war in Ukraine, affecting reservists and former service members and marking a major wartime escalation.","locator":"lines 659-661 and 674","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous news report on the mobilization decree and its scope.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers 21 September 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed directly to Putin as the decree issuer.","contrary_evidence":["Russian officials said the measure was limited and necessary for defense."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.8","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Putin says Russia will not give in to 'blackmail and intimidation'","publisher":"Euronews (Reuters)","publication_date":"2022-09-22","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/09/22/ukraine-crisis-putin","claim":"Reuters reported that Putin, speaking after mobilization, said Russia would not yield to 'blackmail and intimidation' and portrayed the war as a fight to save people in Donbas.","locator":"lines 637-640","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters report on Putin's public wartime framing immediately after mobilization.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers late September 2022 rhetoric and mobilization justification.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed directly to Putin's public justification narrative.","contrary_evidence":["Western and Ukrainian officials described the war as aggression and coercion."],"lenses":["2B.3","2B.6","2B.8"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia calls up 300,000 reservists, says 6,000 soldiers killed in Ukraine","publisher":"Euronews (Reuters)","publication_date":"2022-09-22","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/09/22/ukraine-crisis-putin-mobilisation","claim":"Reuters reported that Russia called up 300,000 reservists after suffering battlefield reverses and that the mobilization was intended to support the war in Ukraine.","locator":"headline and lead summary on the article page","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters report on the mobilization decision and the stated casualty context.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers September 2022 wartime mobilization.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed directly to Putin and the Russian defense leadership.","contrary_evidence":["Russian officials said mobilization was limited and defensive."],"lenses":["2B.8","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia excludes some IT professionals, bankers and journalists from mobilisation","publisher":"Euronews (Reuters)","publication_date":"2022-09-24","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/09/24/ukraine-crisis-mobilisation-exceptions","claim":"Reuters reported that Russia exempted selected IT, finance, and state-media workers from mobilization, showing the decree was selectively shaped around regime and economic priorities rather than a pure across-the-board emergency call-up.","locator":"lines 663-665","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters reporting on the categories exempted from mobilization.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly covers the September 2022 mobilization regime.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Putin's mobilization state policy and the Russian government.","contrary_evidence":["The Kremlin said exemptions were needed to protect critical sectors."],"lenses":["2B.8","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Permanent Mission of the Russian Federation to the United Nations","publisher":"RussiaUN","publication_date":"2022-09-30","url":"https://russiaun.ru/en/news/sc_300922n","claim":"Russia's UN mission defended the September 2022 referenda as lawful and said the accession treaties were signed, rejecting the draft resolution that would have condemned the annexation move and urged diplomatic resolution.","locator":"lines 46-55","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Official Russian mission transcript with explicit legal and diplomatic claims made at the UN.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers the annexation day in September 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Putin-led Russian state policy and diplomatic defense of annexation.","contrary_evidence":["The UN Secretary-General and many member states called the referenda illegal and coercive."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.6","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia-Ukraine war: West says Putin 'being misled' by advisers","publisher":"Al Jazeera","publication_date":"2022-03-30","url":"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2022/3/30/white-house-says-putin-misled-by-advisers-on-ukraine-war","claim":"Al Jazeera reported Western assessments that Putin was being misinformed about the war's performance and that negotiations to end the war had failed to produce results while Russian bombardment continued.","locator":"lines 74-76, 86-90, 101-128","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous reporting that combines official assessments with Reuters reporting about battlefield and negotiation conditions.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly concerns March 2022 decision-making and war continuation.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Putin's decision environment and Russian war leadership.","contrary_evidence":["The Kremlin denied these assessments and maintained the war was going to plan."],"lenses":["2B.6","2B.9","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia denies military forces killed Bucha civilians in Ukraine","publisher":"Al Jazeera","publication_date":"2022-04-04","url":"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2022/4/4/kremlin-rejects-accusation-russian-forces-killed-bucha-civilians","claim":"Al Jazeera reported that the Kremlin rejected responsibility for civilian killings in Bucha and called the evidence fake, even as journalists found corpses in civilian clothing after Russian withdrawal.","locator":"lines 75-92","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous report capturing both the Kremlin denial and the underlying reported civilian deaths.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers a key April 2022 civilian-harm episode.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Russian official denial under Putin's war authority.","contrary_evidence":["International media and Ukrainian authorities reported the bodies as evidence of Russian abuses."],"lenses":["2B.4","2B.9"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia tells UN that Ukraine is preparing to use a dirty bomb","publisher":"Al Jazeera","publication_date":"2022-10-25","url":"https://www.aljazeera.com/amp/news/2022/10/25/russia-tells-un-that-ukraine-is-preparing-to-use-a-dirty-bomb","claim":"Al Jazeera reported that Russia warned the UN Ukraine was preparing a dirty-bomb attack, while Western governments called the claim transparently false and a likely pretext for escalation.","locator":"lines 69-71, 95-100, 104-112","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous Reuters-based reporting on an escalating nuclear-risk narrative and the counterclaims against it.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers the October 2022 escalation environment.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Russian state messaging under Putin's wartime leadership.","contrary_evidence":["The UK, France, the US, and Ukraine rejected the allegation as false and escalation-oriented."],"lenses":["2B.6","2B.8","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia accuses US of 'direct involvement' in Ukraine war","publisher":"Al Jazeera","publication_date":"2022-08-02","url":"https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2022/8/2/russia-accuses-us-of-direct-role-in-war-in-ukraine","claim":"Al Jazeera reported that Russia accused the United States of direct involvement in the war by referencing Ukrainian use of US-supplied HIMARS, extending the conflict narrative to alleged proxy support.","locator":"lines 77-92","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters-based reporting on Russia's official escalation narrative and proxy-blame claims.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly covers August 2022 wartime rhetoric.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Russian defense and diplomatic messaging under Putin.","contrary_evidence":["The article notes the US and Ukraine denied direct US targeting involvement."],"lenses":["2B.5","2B.6","2B.8"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"An emboldened, confident Putin says there will be no peace in Ukraine until Russia's goals are met","publisher":"Associated Press","publication_date":"2023-12-14","url":"https://apnews.com/article/putin-russia-press-conference-moscow-ukraine-ef4e88fda50e6ad75b8a1979b95d9fcc","claim":"AP reported that Putin said there would be no peace in Ukraine until Russia achieves its goals, and that those goals remained the same as when he sent troops in February 2022.","locator":"lines 2289-2290, 2373-2375","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Direct quotation and summary from a major wire service, albeit in a later retrospective setting.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Retrospectively links the 2023 statement back to the 2022 invasion aims.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed directly to Putin's continuing war aims.","contrary_evidence":["Ukraine and Western governments reject the de-Nazification and neutrality framing as false."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.3","2B.7","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"What Putin’s 'Special Ops' Mindset Means for Russia and Ukraine","publisher":"Carnegie Endowment for International Peace","publication_date":"2022-02-23","url":"https://carnegieendowment.org/posts/2022/02/putins-special-ops-mindset-what-next-for-russia-and-ukraine","claim":"Carnegie argued that Putin's recognition of the breakaway territories and military buildup suggested a broader coercive strategy around Ukraine's status and alignment, not a narrow defensive action.","locator":"article body, introductory analysis of Russia's recognition and military buildup","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Expert analysis close to the event date, useful for interpreting strategy and intent but still interpretive.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Pre-invasion analysis directly relevant to 2022 intent.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Putin and the Kremlin's strategic choices.","contrary_evidence":["This is analytical interpretation rather than an official admission or legal finding."],"lenses":["2B.1","2B.2","2B.3","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Russia's Ill-Fated Invasion of Ukraine: Lessons in Modern Warfare","publisher":"CSIS","publication_date":"2022-06-01","url":"https://www.csis.org/analysis/russias-ill-fated-invasion-ukraine-lessons-modern-warfare","claim":"CSIS concluded that Russia failed to achieve most of its objectives in Ukraine and was still attempting a de facto annexation of parts of eastern and southern Ukraine that it controlled.","locator":"The Issue section","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Major policy analysis summarizing battlefield outcomes and occupation strategy, not a legal judgment.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Summarizes the 2022 invasion's first months and their strategic effects.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Putin's war objectives and Russian occupation policy.","contrary_evidence":["Russia said its aims were limited and defensive."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.8","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"How Putin Got the West Wrong","publisher":"Council on Foreign Relations","publication_date":"2022-04-11","url":"https://www.cfr.org/articles/how-putin-got-west-wrong","claim":"CFR argued that Putin expected the invasion to divide the West but instead triggered deeper unity and sanctions, showing a major strategic miscalculation about the consequences of the war.","locator":"opening analysis paragraphs","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"High-quality expert analysis of the strategic consequences of Putin's decision, but not a primary record.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly relevant to the 2022 invasion's strategic end-state.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Putin's strategic choices and miscalculation.","contrary_evidence":["The piece is interpretive and not a legal finding."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.10"]}
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Why Is Putin Upping the Ante in Ukraine?","publisher":"Carnegie Endowment for International Peace","publication_date":"2022-09-21","url":"https://carnegieendowment.org/russia-eurasia/politika/2022/09/why-is-putin-upping-the-ante-in-ukraine","claim":"Carnegie noted that Putin's September 2022 partial mobilization and annexation push transformed the conflict into a war over claiming and defending Russian-held Ukrainian territory.","locator":"opening paragraphs","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Expert analysis from a major policy institute, closely tied to the September 2022 escalation.","final_evidence_use":"context","period_fit":"Directly covers the September 2022 escalation and annexation move.","ruler_attribution":"Attributed to Putin's decision to raise the stakes in the war.","contrary_evidence":["This is analytic framing, not an official legal judgment."],"lenses":["2B.2","2B.8","2B.10"]}

Accepted new evidence: 20 distinct URLs across 11 domains.

Search ledger:
- Candidates found: about 35 plausible documents
- Documents opened: 24 accessible documents
- Duplicates/mirrors/syndicated rewrites consolidated away: 11
- Irrelevant or out-of-period items dropped: 4
- Inaccessible items: 5
- Accepted distinct URLs: 20

Material gaps and next best query/source directions:
1. The strongest remaining gap is direct primary Kremlin text for 21 February 2022, 24 February 2022, and 30 September 2022. Those pages timed out or were unstable in this browser, so the next best step is alternate access to the exact transcripts/decrees and the official video pages.
2. Direct UN Security Council and General Assembly verbatim records from 2022 would tighten the legality and attribution trail for the invasion, annexation, and mobilization sequence.
3. ICC and ICJ direct pages were blocked here. If accessible through another route, they would materially strengthen the legal-finding side of 2B.4 and 2B.9.
4. The chapter still lacks a strong 2B.8 procurement/patronage thread. If you want better coverage there, the next queries should target Russian defense-budget execution, procurement investigations, and sanctions-linked enrichment reporting from 2022.
5. For proxy responsibility, the dossier would benefit from direct reporting on occupation administration, filtration, and deportation chains from UN/NGO investigations with named command responsibility.
